1.0-pre0
* Release: Initial release
1.1
* Add WBMP support and Perl bindings.
1.2
* reduce per-thread stack usage - default was 8Mb on i386 linux. now 256k this makes top output look much nicer ;)
* optimize lcd buffer path, removing a conversion step. and reducing the buffer size from 7k to 1k
* misc other memory optimisations.
* added python bindings (thanks muhgatus)
* added ability for lcd clients to receive L G & M key keypresses directly
* moved lcd display/client switch from L1 to MR
* MR key is now backlit when clients are attached.
* Added ability for lcd clients to change backlight brightness
* Added ability for lcd clients to toggle M-key LEDs
* Added libG15Render client support.
* Added ability for hidden lcd clients to bring themselves to the foreground
* clients change only their own backlight/mkey led status
1.2.1
* Fix bug which could cause client screens to be lost under certain circumstances.
1.2.2
* Vastly improve latency issues when using 'G' keys
* Documentation updates
* includes xkb patch for xorg 7.1 for native g15 keyboard layout in X11 (contrib directory)
1.2.3
* improved the Xmodmaprc configuration, it now has parity with the xkb version
1.2.4
* Users can now choose to use the L1 key to switch between client screens instead of MR.
* L1 is the small round black button directly below the LCD.
* Use -s on the commandline to activate the change.
1.2.5
* Add ability for clients to request all M and G keypresses be 'pushed' to them,
  rather than having to request them repeatedly. If a client uses this option,
  no keyboard processing is done by the daemon, and the client must be prepared
  to do uinput processing itself, if necessary. This limitation may be removed in
  future versions of the API. Normal processing will resume when the client that
  requested this feature exits or closes its connection.
* Add manpage for the daemon.
* Fix automake bug that caused documentation not to be installed by default.
* Fix the daemons cmdline processing to handle more than one commandline option.
* Refactored the code slightly to allow for easier modification in the future.
* Handle long commandline arguments such as --help --version --kill --switch.
* Greatly improve error reporting.
* Add client development documentation (man g15daemon_client_devel / README.client_devel)
* Added a 'debug' mode (-d or --debug) cmdline switch to keep the daemon in the foreground
  rather than daemonising.  All errors and other info will be reported to STDERR in this mode.
* If compiled with libg15 1.1.0 or greater (or svn versions later than 3/11/06), the daemon
  will now reset the keyboard to defaults on exit.
* make distcheck && make dist now work as expected.
* libg15daemon_client is now slightly more useful
* debian packaging now installs manpages
1.2.5svn
* Add compiletime check for uinput version, should resolve compilation problems on some distro's
* Security improved - the daemon now sets its effective uid to nobody as soon as possible.
1.9.0
* Feature: Add plugin API
* Feature: partially rewritten event core
* Feature: updated g15daemon_xmms_spectrum plugin with new features, available in trunk/g15daemon_audio_plugins (SVN)
* Feature: Clock is now a plugin
* Feature: dependency on libdaemon is now removed
* Feature: g15daemon is now dependant on libg15render.
* Feature: Clock now includes analog clock thanks to Rasta Freak <igor.jusic@zg.t-com.hr>
* Moved g15daemon_xmms_spectrum plugin to separate package
1.9.1
* BugFix: Plugins are now installed in ${PREFIX}/{${LIBDIR}/g15daemon/${VERSION}/plugins
* Feature: OS-X support thanks to Fabrizio Sestito.
* Bugfix: libg15daemon_client: keypresses were being corrupted.
* Bugfix: libg15daemon_client: use g15_recv rather than recv.
* Bugfix: use default scheduling for all threads.
* Optimisation: minor optimisation of lcd_cycle() code.
* Security: repair some potential security holes.
* Bugfix: Backlight status was being mis-applied when cycling screens.
* Bugfix: Language bindings were not being distributed.
1.9.2
* BugFix: Add exitfunc to net plugin for exit notification.
* BugFix: Use pause() instead of sleeping
* BugFix: create leaving var as volatile.
* BugFix: Add NAME section to g15daemon_client manpages
* Optimisation: Tweak delay between successive keyboard reads. This reduces cpu load by 50% on my system.
* Bugfix: Ensure that all plugin exit functions are called on leaving.
* Bugfix: if keypress event is received (very early in the startup process,
          the daemon would crash.  Check that expected pointers are valid.
* Bugfix: Dont attempt compilation of uinput plugin if headers are
          unavailable.
* Bugfix: Write a blank buffer to the LCD before exiting.
* Feature: Add --lcdlevel cmdline option to allow setting default LCD brightness level
1.9.3:
* BugFix: The documentation for --switch was inverted. Fix.
* Debug: Print list of commandline args when in debug mode
* BugFix: The decreased delay caused keypresses to be misread on some machines. REVERT.
1.9.4
* Debug: Log warning if keyboard disappears.
* Bugfix: Fix autoconf autodetect bugs re uinput plugin.
* Feature: If autodetection of uinput fails, configure now has a --disable-uinput override.
* Feature: WIP should now compile and run on Linux, MacOSX, and Solaris (v10+).
           Only Linux and Solaris have been tested.
* Debug: Add more debugging to plugin loader.
* Debug: Log build date,OS and GCC version.
* Feature: Plugin loader will now use DEEP_BIND if available, hopefully
           resolving conflicts on OS's that support it.
* Feature: Solaris support. Requires some end-user changes to the usb
           stack at the moment. Documentation coming soon.
* BugFix: Plugin loader is now much more robust.
* Feature: Add OS specific documentation for Linux and FreeBSD.
           Compilation and use on FreeBSD is completely untested.
* Feature: Debug verbosity of g15daemon_log is now variable.
* Feature: Plugin filenames are now cached in g15daemon.conf to allow
           (manual, at this stage) changing of load-order.
* Portability: Add our own daemon() function if platform doesn't have native support.
* TidyUp: Wrap keyboard read function.
* TidyUp:  Make all plugin-internal functions static.
* Portability: Remove mutexes on Solaris, as libusb (and therefore libg15) blocks on read.
* Optimisation: Use pthread conditional variable to signal LCD state change.
* Debug: Further reduces unnecessary wakeups.
1.9.5
* Feature: Add example udev helper scripts to contrib directory.
* API: Add NEVER_SELECT cmd to client API to enforce non-display on
       client-switch.  Used by G15Macro if available.
* Debug: Add segfault handler to libg15daemon_client to aid debugging clients.
* Feature: Add screendump ability.  Pressing M1+M3 simultaneously will write a pbm format image
          of the currently displayed screen to /tmp/g15daemon-sc-?.pbm, where ? is an incremental number.
* BugFix: Only wakeup display thread if LCD buffer is visible.
* Packaging: Fix debian packaging to include plugins.
1.9.5.1:
* BugFix: If lcd refresh is requested whilst processing, refreshes were missed.
* Optimisation: The delay between screen updates is no longer required. remove.
1.9.5.2:
* BugFix: IS_USER_SELECTED client command was broken. fix it.
* BugFix: restore client ability to change backlight state.
1.9.5.3:
* BugFix: plugins/g15daemon_net.c: ensure that OOB traffic is not mixed with
          normal image buffers.
* Feature: Add --set-backlight to allow clients (and the backlight button)
           to set the backlight level for the currently shown screen only.  Default is
           now to disallow clients changing backlight, and to set backlight globally
           via the button.
1.9.5.4
* Fork: Fork and bump version
* BugFix: Most Gentoo and Arch bugfixes applied
1.9.5.5
* BugFix: Adequate files for FreeBSD build properly
1.9.5.6
* Optimisation: Reorganized contrib directory, fixed some typos and added some stuff
1.9.5.7
* BugFix: G-keys working again on FreeBSD
3.0
* Feature: Code revamped. Bumped to a higher version number to clean things up
3.0.1
* BugFix: Removed AC PREREQ
* Documentation: Changed some information in READMEs
3.0.2
* BugFix: Updated config.guess and config.sub. Thanks  Nicolas F. (@CounterPillow)
3.1
* Feature: Backlight is now global instead of per client. CLIENT_CMD_BACKLIGHT sets the LCD level, CLIENT_CMD_KB_BACKLIGHT the keyboard level, and the level is re-applied after a keyboard re-init. --set-backlight is accepted but ignored.
* Feature: New logind plugin (g15plugin_logind, Linux with libdbus-1) replaces g15dpms-monitor. It watches seat0's IdleHint and turns both backlights off while idle without changing which screen is in front (no more blank screen when locked). Optional "Idle Command"/"Active Command"/"Wake Bright" under [Idle Monitor] in g15daemon.conf; commands run unprivileged. Do not run g15dpms-monitor alongside it.
* Feature: Screen priority. Apps are remembered by name in [Screen Priority] in g15daemon.conf (Known.<name>, Last Selected). A new app takes the LCD, but a known app (e.g. g15stats restarting at login) joins behind the screen you last picked with the cycle key. Anonymous clients keep the old always-in-front behaviour. Saved at clean shutdown only.
* Feature: When the screen in front disconnects, the LCD returns to the screen it covered instead of its list neighbour, so popups (g15notifications, g15media) no longer leave g15stats in front. Popups ask for the foreground with CLIENT_CMD_SWITCH_PRIORITIES and hand it back when they close; stacked popups unwind to the original screen.
* Feature: Connected clients are identified by process name (from /proc), used for screen priority and logging. Under systemd this needs CAP_SYS_PTRACE and CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH from the unit file (contrib/init/g15daemon.service) - with an older installed unit every client shows as "peer <ip>:<port>" and screen choices are not saved.
* Feature: systemd integration - sd_notify READY/STATUS/WATCHDOG, so "systemctl status g15daemon" shows version, uptime, client count, foreground screen and LCD draw time. Needs NotifyAccess=main and WatchdogSec= in the installed unit.
* Feature: Clock plugin. L2 cycles digital, digital with seconds (HH:MM:SS, no seconds bar) and analog, L3 toggles the date, L4 no longer does anything (it used to switch digital/analog; the old L2 toggled 12/24h). 12/24h now follows the locale instead of a key, with "Locale:" (empty = daemon's environment, e.g. nb_NO.UTF-8 for local day/month names) and "Time Format: Auto|12h|24h" under [Clock]. The old 24hrFormat key is ignored. Accented letters in day/month names are shown as plain ASCII. The digital clock shows the seconds as a line across the top pixel row that fills smoothly over each minute ("Seconds Bar: Off" disables it). The clock redraws every 100ms so seconds change on time, but only pushes frames that changed, and no longer flickers from a buffer cleared mid-draw.
* Change: Logging uses standard syslog severities. Without -d, NOTICE and above go to syslog/journal; -d/-d 1 sends the same to stderr, -d 2 adds INFO (client connect/disconnect with name, PID, peer and duration; registered-client list; startup timing), -d 3 adds DEBUG. Under journald stderr lines carry their priority.
* BugFix: Concurrency fixes for the libg15 kernel-driver backend: separate mutexes for keys and LCD/LEDs (idle key polling starved LCD writes for seconds), a startup race leaving a client node with NULL info, and a use-after-free from a dangling last_priority pointer.
* BugFix: g15daemon.conf was written at shutdown from the already freed client list; it is now written first.
* BugFix: Assorted overflow, memory-leak, sequence-point and unchecked-return-value fixes (clock, plugin loader, config writer, uinput plugin, client library).
3.1.1
* BugFix: Digital clock spacing - colon and hour "1" no longer sit in full-width cells (even 3px gaps), digits and AM/PM centred on what is drawn
* Change: "New screen registered" is logged at NOTICE only the first time an app joins per run; repeat joins (popups reconnecting for every toast) at INFO
* Change: systemd status says "N connection events since start" instead of the misleading "N total"
* Change: Backlights are no longer forced to a level at startup. Set "LCD Backlight"/"Keyboard Backlight" (0-2) under [Global] or use -l; otherwise the current level is kept
* BugFix: The systemd status showed the last level g15daemon wrote, not the real one. With libg15 3.0.9 the levels are read back every 5s and outside changes (light key, UPower/GNOME) are adopted and logged at INFO, so waking from idle restores the real level
* Change: The LCD backlight is no longer switched off when g15daemon exits (only the screen is blanked); SIGUSR1 still switches both backlights off
* Feature: The logind plugin switches the LCD backlight off when the system powers off or reboots (PrepareForShutdown, with a delay inhibitor lock so it happens before shutdown continues)
* Change: The logind plugin only darkens the LCD backlight on idle; the keyboard backlight is left to UPower/GNOME (idle) and systemd-backlight (poweroff/boot), which it raced - it could save GNOME's 0 and write it back on wake, and darkening it at poweroff made it come back off after boot. Wake Bright now only applies to the LCD
* Change: The logind plugin's idle/wake messages are logged at NOTICE, with the saved/restored LCD level
* BugFix: The LCD level is read back right before going dark for idle/poweroff, so waking restores a level changed just before
* Change: The light key (libusb backend only) cycles just the LCD backlight; the keyboard light is left to the hardware/UPower
3.1.2
* BugFix: g15daemon.conf values are split on the first ":"/"=" only, so commands like "env DISPLAY=:0 ..." are no longer cut short (and written back cut short at shutdown); "]" inside a value no longer starts a section; a symlinked conf is read in full; a lone "]" line no longer overflows a buffer
* BugFix: An unplugged keyboard no longer blocks the LCD thread (and with it the systemd watchdog, which killed the daemon after 30s); the watchdog is also pinged when the screen in front does not update
* BugFix: Shutdown waits (up to 5s) for plugin and client threads before freeing the client list, instead of freeing it under still-running client threads
* BugFix: SIGPIPE is ignored, so a key press as a client disconnects can no longer kill the daemon when run outside systemd (OpenRC/runit/66 scripts, -d from a shell)
* BugFix: Thread-safety: key presses are dispatched with the client list locked (a disconnecting popup could free the screen being sent a key), redraw requests use a proper mutex and are coalesced, and a client socket is closed only after its screen is removed (keys could go to a reused fd)
* Change: At most 10 TCP clients (MAX_CLIENTS) are accepted at once; further connections are closed and logged. It was only the listen backlog before, so any local process could open unlimited screens
* BugFix: /dev/uinput is opened before the privilege drop; the uinput plugin no longer switches the whole process back to root at runtime (other threads ran as root meanwhile, and the daemon stayed root if uinput could not be opened)
* BugFix: g15daemon.conf is only rewritten at shutdown when something changed, and then via a temp file, fsync and rename (a symlinked conf stays a symlink), so a power cut during poweroff can no longer leave it empty; write errors are now detected
* BugFix: The foreground screen's M-key LEDs no longer overwrite those set by a client key handler (macro recorder)
* BugFix: M1-M3 key LED writes are serialized with the other LCD/LED writes
* BugFix: libg15daemon_client: a command answer that doesn't arrive returns -1 as documented (IS_FOREGROUND returned -48, i.e. true, so popups thought they were in front); the wait is 1s instead of 100ms
* BugFix: A failed accept() no longer registers a phantom client with fd -1
* BugFix: If a client thread can't be started, its screen is removed again instead of staying in the list (blank, possibly in front) forever
* BugFix: WBMP ('W') client buffers: images taller than the LCD no longer put the stream out of step, the width is decoded as a WBMP multi-byte integer, and short reads end the connection
* BugFix: The cycle key no longer hangs the daemon when every screen is marked never-select
* Change: Removed the unused keyhandler/client_handles_keys code
* Change: generic_info is declared with its real type
* BugFix: A stale pidfile whose pid now belongs to another process no longer stops g15daemon from starting; pidfile errors are logged
* BugFix: Exit signals are blocked in all threads and taken with sigwait() by the main thread, so a SIGTERM while plugins are still loading no longer kills the daemon without cleanup
* BugFix: Idle Command/Active Command no longer keep root's supplementary groups
* BugFix: The plugin load order is rebuilt when a plugin it names no longer exists, not only when the number of plugins changes
* BugFix: A broken or incompatible plugin .so is skipped with an error instead of crashing the daemon
* BugFix: L1 tap-vs-hold timing uses a monotonic clock, so a clock change can't turn a tap into a hold
* BugFix: The systemd status line is no longer cut off with long foreground screen names
* BugFix: ';' comments containing ':' or '=' (e.g. the shipped "; Locale: ..." notes) are no longer cut off when g15daemon.conf is written back
* BugFix: Key events are sent to clients whole or not at all (a partial non-blocking write could misalign every later key), and a client that doesn't read its keys no longer logs a warning per key press
* BugFix: With the Clock plugin disabled or missing, cycling to the empty default screen no longer crashes the daemon, and G-keys still work while it is in front
* BugFix: Switching screens (cycle key or a priority request) applies the new screen's own contrast and M-key LEDs